%% DM26-0670

%% Built (2026-11-04, configuration-flow.md, policy-enforcement.md); the shaded part is designed (policy-enforcement.md, stage 6), not built. polar-init's part is
%% general/workload_certificate_issuance. What the agent asks for next is general/configuration_replay. An agent that refuses its own settings is
%% general/held_agent_and_dynamic_setting.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant KL as Kubelet
    participant PI as polar-init (init container)
    participant AG as Agent process (run)
    participant PE as polar-env (Config)
    participant DS as Domain supervisor
    participant AB as AgentBuilder
    participant IS as InfrastructureSupervisor

    KL->>PI: start, with --cert and --check-dep-cert arguments
    PI->>PI: wait for the dependencies' certificates, get the custody daemon's custodian its certificate
    PI->>PI: the custodian fetches this agent's certificates into the daemon, which keeps their keys
    opt the agent needs encryption (POLAR_INIT_ESCROW_BOOTSTRAP)
        PI->>PI: the custodian also fetches the escrow key, which the daemon keeps
    end
    PI->>PI: leave the start marker, for a pod that restarts in place
    PI-->>KL: exit 0
    KL->>AG: start, with the environment the resolver derived
    AG->>PE: a snapshot of the process environment, declared variables only
    PE-->>AG: values with their sources: env, default, unset
    AG->>AG: judge it: capabilities the code requires against POLAR_CAPABILITIES, each section's variables and relations
    alt any problem
        AG-->>KL: every problem together, exit 1
    end
    AG->>AG: take the start marker. None there: restarted alone, exit 1 (pod_restart_in_place)
    AG->>AG: judge its declared commands, and the workloads it serves
    AG->>AG: the topic set: TOPICS declared, plus implied (the builder's own topics, those NEEDS bring),<br/>the same set --scaffold prints, each implied topic with its rule
    AG->>DS: start(Configured), with the Config
    DS->>DS: read its own settings from the snapshot
    alt they cannot work, and a restart would not help
        DS->>DS: held::stay_up instead, infrastructure only
    end
    DS->>AB: build()
    AB->>AB: the service name must be the workload its certificate names, else refuse to start
    AB->>IS: spawn: health, configuration, authority, router, subscriptions, Cassini client,<br/>crypto, state, protocol handlers, commands, as the agent needs them
    IS-->>DS: AgentResources, including the same Config
    Note over IS: Every subscribe and publish is judged<br/>before it leaves: Cedar first,<br/>then the topic set (topic_gate)
    IS->>IS: on each Registered: tell crypto<br/>and the authority, ask for<br/>the signed documents<br/>(configuration_replay)

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over AB,IS: DESIGNED (policy-enforcement.md, stage 6), not built
    IS->>IS: not healthy until a snapshot from<br/>the credentials agent is verified<br/>(a bootstrap service is: it runs on<br/>the certificate floor until its first)
    end
